/* MD5, because bilibili's TV login endpoints want a signed request.
 *
 * `sign` is md5(sorted urlencoded query + appsec). There is no crypto API worth
 * relying on in this engine — SubtleCrypto needs a secure context and a widget
 * loaded from file:// is not one — so the digest is computed here.
 *
 * Verified against the RFC 1321 test vectors by tools/md5-verify.mjs. It handles
 * whole bytes only, which is all a signature string ever contains, but the UTF-8
 * step is kept so a stray non-ASCII parameter cannot silently produce a digest
 * that differs from what the server computes.
